\foreach \x in {0,...,4} {\draw (\x,0.12)--(\x,-0.12);}
\node[below] at (0,-0.12) {$0.24$};
\node[below] at (4,-0.12) {$0.32$};
\fill (1,0) circle (2.2pt); \node[above] at (1,0.15) {$S$};
\fill (3,0) circle (2.2pt); \node[above] at (3,0.15) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) The whole gap is $0.32-0.24=0.08$.
Half the gap is $0.04$.
$0.24+0.04=0.28$
(b) Each interval is $0.08\div4=0.02$.
$S=0.26$ and $T=0.30$.
$T$ is to the right of $S$, so $T$ is greater.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0);
\foreach \x in {0,...,4} {\draw (\x,0.12)--(\x,-0.12);}
\node[below] at (0,-0.12) {$0.24$};
\node[below] at (4,-0.12) {$0.32$};
\fill (1,0) circle (2.2pt); \node[above] at (1,0.15) {$S$};
\fill (2,0) circle (2.2pt); \node[above] at (2,0.15) {$0.28$};
\fill (3,0) circle (2.2pt); \node[above] at (3,0.15) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

