workedExamples.solution_text:
There are $3$ intervals between the two known labels.
$4.722-4.710=0.012$
$0.012\div3=0.004$ per interval.
There are $6$ intervals from the left endpoint to the right endpoint.
$4.710+6\times0.004=4.734$
The right endpoint is $4.734$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.5,0);
\foreach \x in {0,...,6} {\draw (\x,0.12)--(\x,-0.12);}
\node[below] at (0,-0.12) {$4.710$};
\node[below] at (6,-0.12) {$4.734$};
\fill (3,0) circle (2.2pt); \node[above] at (3,0.15) {$4.722$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

